NAMp — a four-channel Neural Amp Modeler amp head, as a plug-in and as a program,
with five pedals alongside them.
Copyright (c) 2026 rations

This file covers everything this repository releases:

  NAMp Rations    the amp head as a plug-in. VST3 for Linux, Windows and macOS;
                  LV2 for Linux; a five-pedal pedalboard built in.
  NAMp Rack       the amp as its own program for Linux and Windows, hosting other
                  people's plug-ins around it. VST3 and LV2 on Linux; VST3 only on
                  Windows.
  Rations Pedals  five stompboxes as separate VST3 plug-ins, shipped with NAMp Rack
                  and also released on their own.

This project builds on NeuralAmpModelerPlugin by Steven Atkinson, and directly on the
author's own NAMp and NAMix. The original upstream project is available at:
  https://github.com/sdatkinson/NeuralAmpModelerPlugin

The project's own code — the VST3 and LV2 integrations, the plug-in host, the chain
engine, the crossfade and channel-switch engines and the editor — is released under
the MIT Licence; see LICENSE. The third-party components it links, vendors and
redistributes are covered by the licences below.

WHERE A SECTION APPLIES TO ONLY ONE PRODUCT, IT SAYS SO. Everything else applies to
both, because both are built from one amp in one tree.

