Amp captures and impulse responses:

  This project ships NO captures, contains none, and claims no rights over any.
  Each of the four banks is a folder or a file the user loads for themselves, and a
  fresh instance comes up with four empty channels. The same is true of the cabinet
  page's impulse responses.

  A .nam capture is a recording of an amplifier, made by whoever trained it and
  distributed under whatever terms they set. It is not source, this project's MIT
  grant says nothing about one, and none is redistributed here in any form.

  The offline proofs need capture banks to run against and are pointed at a local
  set by command-line option or environment variable. Those files belong to their
  own authors; pointing a development gate at them puts them under no grant from
  this project and implies no permission to redistribute them.

